{title: I Will Not Let You Go}
{subtitle: Genesis 32:22–32}
{key: Gm}
{tempo: 72}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Gm] | ×9

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
I sent my wives and children across the Jabbok ford
I sent the gift on ahead of me, every flock and herd
Then I was left alone there on the river bank that night
A [C]man came out of the darkness and he wrestled me till light
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Gm]I will not let you go unless you bless me
Wrestled all night long until the day was breaking
[C]He touched my hip and wrenched it but I'm holding on
I will not let you go unless you [Gm]bless me
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
He asked me what's your name, I said Jacob is my name
The heel-grab-ber, the schemer, the man who carried shame
[C]Your name will no longer be Jacob, but Israel
You have struggled with God and with men and have prevailed
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
I named that place Peniel
I have seen God face to face
And yet my life was spared
The sun rose above him as he passed Penuel
And he was [C]limping because of his [Gm]hip
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Limping in the sunrise
Blessed and holding on
[C]I will not let you go
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Interlude}
| [Gm] | [Gm] | [Gm] | [Gm] |
| [C] | [C] | [C] | [C] |
| [Gm] | [Gm] | [Gm] | [Gm] |
